# The scanned leaves: ~180 MB, and they are regenerated in two commands
# from the two original PDFs (see README, § 2). "Livret explicatif.pdf"
# is 114 MB and exceeds GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit in any case.
scan/

# LaTeX output.
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
essai.*
altezo.*
chaso.*
noto.*

# Working images produced by tools/reading.py.
tools/.reading/
__pycache__/

# The wall plates: the original PDFs weigh close to 100 MB, and the two
# extracted layers as much again. Only the two WebP per table, which
# tools/plates.py draws from them, are versioned -- about 1 MB each.
plates/font/
plates/working/

# The cleaned scan: it is remade in one command from the versioned
# facsimile (tools/originals.py clean), and weighs eight times as much.
originals/working/

# Working sheets for the survey by eye: the tiles of manual.py and the
# proofing sheet of ciphers.py. They are remade in one command, and what
# is kept of them goes into plates/manual.json.
plates/tiles/
plates/proposals.png
plates/proposals.json
